{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>But you shall come to your fathers in peace</b> — and you shall not see any of all this; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 15:15). But it is not correct according to his own interpretation, for he said (Genesis 15:13), 'for your seed shall be a stranger' — from the time that you have seed, and from the time Isaac was born, it is said of him, 'and Abraham sojourned in the land of the Philistines' (Genesis 21:34), 'and Isaac sojourned in Gerar' — if so, he too is included in the decree. Rather, the meaning of 'but you shall come to your fathers in peace' is that no punishment of any matter shall reach you from Me, even though I decree punishments upon your children through servitude and affliction."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:47.356927612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}